@startuml SysSimX_Execution

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam participantPadding 100
skinparam wrapWidth 0
skinparam maxMessageSize 500

actor User 
participant "System" as System 
participant "Component A\n(e.g., Controller)" as CompA 
participant "Component B\n(e.g., Pendulum)" as CompB 
participant "Connection\nManager" as Connection


== Initialization Phase ==

User -> System: **initialize(t0)**
activate System

System -> CompA: initialize(t0)
activate CompA
CompA -> CompA: _initialize_component(t0)
CompA -> CompA: _update_output_states(t0)
note right: Write initial outputs\nto PortState
CompA --> System: outputs ready
deactivate CompA

System -> CompB: initialize(t0)
activate CompB
CompB -> CompB: _initialize_component(t0)
CompB -> CompB: _update_output_states(t0)
CompB --> System: outputs ready
deactivate CompB

System -> System: build_graphs()
note right: Construct full graph\nand zero-delay DAG
System -> System: compute_execution_order()
note right: Topological generations\n[[CompA], [CompB]]

System --> User: system initialized
deactivate System

== Simulation Loop: step(t, dt) ==

User -> System: **run(t0, tf, dt)**
activate System

loop while t < tf

    note over System: **Phase 1: Set Inputs**\n(for all generations)

    System -> Connection: get signals for CompB
    activate Connection
    Connection -> CompA: outputs['y'].get()
    note right: Read from PortState
    CompA --> Connection: value
    Connection --> System: {port: value}
    deactivate Connection
    
    System -> CompB: **set_inputs(signals, t)**
    activate CompB
    CompB -> CompB: inputs['u'].set(value, t)
    CompB --> System: inputs set
    note right: Store in PortState
    deactivate CompB

    note over System: **Phase 2: Compute**\n(for all generations)

    System -> CompA: **do_step(t, dt)**
    activate CompA
    CompA -> CompA: _do_step_internal(t, dt)
    note right: FMU doStep / FEM solve\nOpenSim integrate / etc.
    CompA -> CompA: _update_output_states(t+dt)
    note right: Write new outputs\n+ append to history
    CompA --> System: step complete
    deactivate CompA
    
    System -> CompB: **do_step(t, dt)**
    activate CompB
    CompB -> CompB: _do_step_internal(t, dt)
    CompB -> CompB: _update_output_states(t+dt)
    CompB --> System: step complete
    deactivate CompB

    System -> System: t += dt

end

System --> User: simulation complete
deactivate System

@enduml